==Old Norse==

===Etymology===
An accusative form of {{term|heimr||abode, world, land|lang=non}}.

===Adverb===
{{infl|non|adverb}}
# [[home]], [[homewards]]
#: ''Flosi var allra manna glaðastr ok beztr '''[[sækja heim#Old Norse|heim]]''' at [[sækja heim#Old Norse|sækja]].''
#:: Flosi was most cheerful of all men and the best to [[visit]].

====Derived terms====
* [[bæta heim fyrir sér]] (to make for one's soul's weal)
* [[bjóða heim]] (to bid one to a feast, ''confer'' '''[[heimboð]]''')
* [[fara heim]] (to return home, to go home)
* [[fara heim á leið]]
* [[sækja heim]] (to visit, to attack somebody)

